<script>
  document.querySelectorAll(".accordion").forEach((accordion) => {
    accordion.querySelectorAll("details").forEach((details) => {
      details.addEventListener("toggle", () => {
        accordion.classList.add("accordion--animated");
      });
    });
  });
</script>
<div id="accordion-css">
  <h1>Accordion CSS Component</h1>
  <p>
    An accordion is a series of expandable sections of content. Each section has
    a summary header that is used to toggle the display of its related content.
  </p>

  <h2>Default Accordion</h2>
  <p>
    By default, each section is rendered as closed. When opened, the section
    will stay open until explicitly closed.
  </p>
  <component-demo component="accordion" variant="closed"/>

  <h2>Opened Accordion</h2>
  <p>
    Apply the <code>open</code> property to render a section in an open state.
  </p>
  <component-demo component="accordion" variant="open"/>

  <h2>Large Accordion</h2>
  <p>
    Apply the <code>accordion--large</code> modifier to increase the size of
    each section summary.
  </p>
  <component-demo component="accordion" variant="large"/>

  <h2>Auto-Collapsing Accordion</h2>
  <p>
    Use the <code>name</code> attribute to ensure only one section can be open
    at a time, with other sections automatically closing.
  </p>
  <p>
    <b>NOTE:</b> For browsers that do not yet support this attribute, Javascript
    is needed to mimic the behavior as a fallback.
  </p>
  <component-demo component="accordion" variant="autoCollapse"/>

  <h2>Accordion with Leading Icon</h2>
  <p>
    To add a leading icon inside the details use <code>details__leading</code>
  </p>
  <component-demo component="accordion" variant="leadingIconClosed"/>

  <h2 id="accordion-animation">Accordion Animation <sup>EXPERIMENTAL</sup></h2>
  <p>
    The accordion features smooth animations with progressive enhancement when
    expanding and collapsing content sections. This is an experimental feature
    that may not be supported in all browsers.
  </p>
  <p>
    To enable all animations, add <code>accordion--animated</code> class. This
    should be added after the user interacts with the component in order to
    prevent animations from triggering when the component is rendered.
  </p>
  <p>
    The accordion uses modern CSS features like
    <code>interpolate-size: allow-keywords</code> that enable smooth transitions
    for intrinsic size values and
    <code>transition-behavior: allow-discrete</code> to allow smoother
    transitions for discrete properties like <code>content-visibility</code> .
  </p>
</div>
